=== intro

The jumpgate appears on sensors as it should—a massive 
ring of alien-derived technology, promising instant 
transit across light-years.

Then you get closer and see the truth.

It's broken. The ring is shattered, fragments spinning 
slowly in the void. Whatever happened here, the gate 
won't be opening again.

* [Investigate the damage]
  ~ fuel -= 3
  -> investigate

* [Salvage what you can]
  -> salvage

* [Log it and continue]
  ~ chronicle "Broken Gate"
    Found a destroyed jumpgate. Another connection severed. Logged and moved on.
  -> END

=== investigate

The damage patterns tell a story. Not impact—the fragments 
would be different. Not age—the materials should last 
millennia. Something overloaded the gate's systems. Something 
made it tear itself apart.

The Cataclysm? A Sera attack? Sabotage? The wreckage 
holds no answers.

But there's something in the debris. A navigation buoy, 
still broadcasting. Still trying to guide ships to a 
gate that no longer exists.

* [Shut down the buoy]
  ~ integrity += 3
  ~ chronicle "Broken Gate"
    Found a destroyed jumpgate. Shut down the navigation buoy. No one should look for this anymore.
  -> END

* [Leave it broadcasting]
  ~ flag broken_gate_logged
  ~ chronicle "Broken Gate"
    Found a destroyed jumpgate. Left the buoy running. Maybe someone will investigate.
  -> END

=== salvage

Jumpgate materials are valuable—the alloys alone are 
worth significant credits. You pick through the debris, 
harvesting what you can.

It feels wrong, somehow. Like grave robbing. But the 
gate's not using the material anymore.

* [Take the components]
  ~ credits += 60
  ~ chronicle "Broken Gate"
    Salvaged components from a destroyed jumpgate. The gate won't miss them.
  -> END

* [Leave it intact]
  ~ integrity += 2
  ~ chronicle "Broken Gate"
    Found a destroyed jumpgate. Couldn't bring myself to salvage it.
  -> END
